{"text": "Polaroid's Newest--'The Swinger\u2019\nBoston Globe (1960-1979); Jul 14, 1965;\n\npg. 18\n\nA less-than-$20 Polaroid\n\u2018Land camera that\u2019 literaily\nsays \u201cyes\u201d in the viewfinder\nwhen the exposure setting is\nerfect to take a 10-second\nlack-and-white picture, wag\nannounced by Polaroid Cor-\nporation Tuesday.\nThe new Model 20 Land\nCamera, to be called \u2018The\nSwinger,\u201d marks Polaroid\u2019s\n\u2018entry in to the mass market\nswith a camera priced in the\nTange which represents 70\npercent of the nation\u2019s cam-\nera volume.\nFirst sales of The Swinger ;\nwill be in retail stores in Can-\n\u2018ada starting July 24. The on-\n\u2018sale date in the United States\nhas not been set firmly yet,\nput according to Polaroid na-\n\ntional sales manager Tom\nPeirce, it might be mid-Sep-\ntember. \u201cIntroduction of the\nnew camera in the U.S.A,,\u201d he\nsaid, \u201cwould be determined\nprimarily by the date Pola-\nroid catches up with the \u2018runa-\nway success\u2019 of the two new-\nest Polaroid color pack cam-\neras that were introduced last\nSpring.\n\u201cDespite the fact that we\nhave doubled production of\nour color pack camera since\n\nPolaroid\u2019s Newest\u2014\u2018The Swinger\u2019\n\nApril 1, we still have not \u00b0\ncaught up with the demand\nand it appears now it will be\nlate August or early Septem- :\nber before our production can -\nmeet the demand. \u2018\n\u201cTo introduce The Swinger\nat this time,\u201d he said, \u201cwould \u00a9\nadd confusion to our distribu-\n\ntion and wo have elected to \u00b0\n\nwait so we can launch this -\nnew inexpensive camera in\nthe U.S.A, in a more orderly\nfashion,\n\nReproduced with permission of the copyright owner. Further reproduction prohibited without permission.",
